ell  actually we are struggling for  establishing democracy  and people's emancipation that's what i  would love to talk with you about prime  minister  so what would you like to accomplish  within these next five years  food security accommodation education  health care job opportunity these are  basic needs then definitely  every human being want a better life  then we have to ensure that  my father struggled his whole life for  this  people and the country he liberted the  country he wanted to build up this  country as a prosperous country but  he could do it so i feel that  this is my job but when you're talking  about establishing a democracy there's  more you want to establish it's like  freedom of speech is  human rights it's gender equality what  are you going to do in this regard  listen actually  what you see now in the country  it is not like this as because our  country  ruled by military dictator time and  again no  movement freedom of movement that was  the situation  we had only one television  no private television no private  radio how people can exercise their  freedom of space  so you say you're coming really actually  i bring a lot of change  1996 when i first time i became prime  minister  first thing i decided that i will open  up  everything to the private sector  one thing is to ensure freedom of speech  and show people's freedom of movement  and right  and our first priority was  to ensure food security  so can't it become self-sufficient in  food  then education  that is also very very important because  unless you educate people how can you  build up this country as a poverty free  country the prime minister would you  consider education one of your priority  priorities we took initiative that we  should ensure that  each and every one should get food  security and  side-by-side education we started  building  schools where there is no school and  also  encourage children to go to school we  started giving mother some  money or some facilities so that  she should send their children to the  school so that  we encourage them for education and for  health care we  started establishing community health  care center  what i feel that their  basic needs their food shelter education  then job opportunity that is also  and also security so it is their  human rights which role does freedom of  speech play for you  you just said that earlier on there were  only state ruled media this is changing  in your country  is it like um also a basic need that  people have the freedom of expression  oh yes of course they can and you  support that 100  100 also critical voices who who  criticize your  your style of leadership or your  decisions would you say this is part of  a democracy  listen if you work more then you will  hear more criticism but  you should ask my people whether they  are satisfied or not  what they think whether they  are getting all what they need  whether i can i mean provide  this we all remember i think the world  does as well  the situation of bloggers here in  bangladesh some years ago  many of them got murdered and killed on  the streets  well some incident happened but  immediately we took action  now you know the  [Music]  terrorism become a worldwide problem  and bangladesh also  face some extent but immediately we take  action  we declare zero tolerance to terrorism  and we we could have controlled that  yeah  how do you do that i mean zero tolerance  it sounds so easy to do  it's it's not that easy it is very  complicated it is true  but what i did  well in one hand i strengthened our law  enforcement agencies  and we train them and special  arrangement for them but what is more  effective  that is i just directly  i go to the people i call upon the  people  but um besides the awareness you needed  to build a coalition with  fundamentalist groups like hifasata  islam during the election  so do they want something out of that  now i told you that in this country  everybody has freedom of 