ern and of course we'll do that  i would like to come one more time back  to the uh elections  which just happened your ruling  coalition won 288 out of 300 seats  that's  96 that's nearly 100 what happened to  the opposition  actually you see when you contest  election what people want to see  who is the leader they couldn't present  that  actually their lack of politics is  mainly there that  they couldn't present any leadership  that who will run the country next  secularism is under threat in your  country  no no you wouldn't say so so you're not  afraid of  like really islamistic forces islamist  forces are there no doubt about it but  ah  if you can see the condition in this  country we have religion harmony  each every religion people they can  perform there  but people get killed on the streets  because of criticizing  or not living conform uh  some religious ideas it is not true they  got threatened  i mean we were talking about bloggers  earlier on i mean this there's a danger  in the streets isn't it  yes i told you that few incidents took  place but immediately we took  you know a step then it stopped  in our country we always  create atmosphere that each and every  religion  they can perform their religion faith  peacefully  honorably secularism doesn't mean that  no religion no we believe in religion  and everybody should have their right  and  we have religious harmony so you don't  feel any threat  islam is a religion for peace  now some only few people sometimes they  use  it but that is the wrong way they  shouldn't do it  prime minister thank you so very much  indeed  you

